# Colour

civica uses the GOV.UK colour palette, unchanged. It was designed with accessibility in mind, but you are still responsible for meeting WCAG when you combine colours. Never use colour alone to give meaning: add a label, an icon, a pattern or text.

## Palette overview

The palette has 4 tiers.

### Primary

Blue is the core colour. The other primary colours show tone, emphasis or a difference between things.

### Tints

Tints are lighter versions of a colour, made by adding white. Use them for backgrounds, highlights and space.

### Shades

Shades are darker versions of a colour, made by adding black. Use them for depth, contrast, and for text or emphasis.

### Accents

Use accents sparingly, to highlight something, add energy, or show an action or a status.


